**TL;DR — 3 Mistakes That Cost $28,000**

1. Choosing VS2 clarity at 3ct (8mm face-up amplifies every inclusion — VS2 that was eye-clean at 2ct shows at 3ct)
2. H color in white gold at 3ct (at 8mm face-up, H reads warm against white metal — G is the minimum)
3. Overlooking the D-IF lab path ($8,849 vs $36,991 — same face-up, same certified grades, $28,142 gap)

A 3 carat asscher cut diamond ring costs between **$9,709 and $41,512** for a complete certified ring in {{month_year}}.

That spread is not random. It reflects real differences in origin, clarity, color, and setting — not quality tiers that look different face-up.

This guide shows you exactly which stones are worth buying, which are not, and why the $28,000 gap exists.

