## Natural Diamonds: What Certified 3ct Asscher Actually Costs

GIA-certified natural asscher cut diamonds at 3ct are among the rarest certified stones in the market.

The cutting geometry of rough asscher crystals does not yield 3ct cleanly. Most natural asschers at this weight require exceptional rough — large, inclusion-free material that commands extraordinary prices at the mine level. What reaches the certified market is priced accordingly.

**[GIA 3.26ct F-VVS2 at $36,991](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — F color is one step from colorless, visually indistinguishable from D or E in a finished ring. VVS2 clarity is invisible to the naked eye and nearly impossible to find even at 10x. At 3.26ct the face-up is approximately 8.2mm — slightly larger than a true 3ct.

This is the entry point for a certified natural 3ct asscher. The price is real — and justified by genuine rarity.

**[GIA 3.08ct D-VS2 at $40,322](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/22270906?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — D color is exceptional. VS2 at 3ct in an asscher carries inclusion risk discussed under Mistake 1. This stone costs $3,331 more than the F-VVS2 and has lower clarity. The D color premium is real, but VS2 at this face-up size requires careful vetting before purchase.

