## How Big Does a 3 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Look?

A 3ct asscher cut measures approximately 8.0mm × 8.0mm face-up. This is the size where the asscher becomes unmistakably large on any finger.

| Carat | Face-Up Size |
|---|---|
| 1.5ct asscher | ~6.5mm |
| 2.0ct asscher | ~7.0mm |
| 2.5ct asscher | ~7.5mm |
| 3.0ct asscher | ~8.0mm |
| 3.26ct asscher | ~8.2mm |

**What this means:** The jump from 2ct to 3ct is 1mm of face-up width — visible and significant. At 8mm the asscher fills the center of a size 6 finger completely. On a size 7 or 8 finger it still reads prominently without appearing too large.

The 3.26ct GIA natural at 8.2mm is slightly larger than a true 3ct. At these sizes a 0.2mm difference is not visible on the finger but shows in the measurement.

